{
 "note": "The private half of tests/data/map_pictures_mutants.json (tools/mutate.py runs it together with the public half): the mutants of files that are not in the public repository, and the ones that only a test that is not there catches. Mutants of the pictures of the players' maps (src/ants_app/png_encode.cpp, map_thumbnail.cpp, src/ants_server/map_pictures.cpp and the three places that ask for a picture: submissions.cpp, test_maps.cpp and the door in control.cpp) for tools/mutate.py (docs/TESTING.md, 'Mutation checks'). Run from the checkout with a configured build folder: python3 tools/mutate.py tests/data/map_pictures_mutants.json --keep-going --jobs 1 --timeout 600. Every mutant must be caught: each breaks one rule of docs/MAP_SUBMISSIONS.md, 'Pictures' (a picture that every PNG reader decodes, the same picture as the setup screen's, what the server keeps and refuses, one picture maker at a time with a time limit and nothing of the server's in it, a map that is sent, approved or tried gets its picture asked for). The case test_map_pictures runs the real picture maker too, so the build line has ants_thumb. The mutants of the program's own limits and of its sandbox (program_limit_*, sandbox_*, child_outlives_the_server, map_parsed_before_the_sandbox) are Linux code (RLIMIT_AS is not enforced on macOS, Landlock, seccomp and the parent-death signal are Linux only): run them in a Linux build (docs/TESTING.md, the pictures row). child_keeps_the_servers_priority needs a test run that is not itself started with a nice value of 10 or more.",
 "baseline": [
